Entries for the Hawaii QSO Party used by in-state (Hawaii) stations
The 14 Hawaii districts (each its own multiplier), the US states but Hawaii, DC on its own, and the 13 Canadian provinces and territories.
DXCC entities other than the USA, Canada, Hawaii and Alaska are the class's DX multiplier, not entries here.
The district file comes FIRST, so a district code wins over any state or province alias spelled the same.
Hawaii is no state multiplier (a Hawaii station sends its district), so s48.dom and alaska.dom are included and s50.dom (which adds hawaii.dom) is not.
The rules count "US states (including DC)": dc.dom is included and DC is a multiplier of its own.
s48.dom comes before p13.dom so LA stays Louisiana. NF and LB are read as NL (the last line).
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

INCLUDE FILE hawaiiqp_cty.dom
INCLUDE FILE s48.dom
INCLUDE FILE alaska.dom
INCLUDE FILE dc.dom
INCLUDE FILE p13.dom
Nl = NF,LB
